{
  "original_id": "primary-20260914-stirling-transition",
  "archive_id": "BW2-PR20260914-stirling_transition",
  "title": "The log-concavity to log-convexity transition in fixed columns of Stirling numbers",
  "batch_label": "primary",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "Let c(n,k) count permutations of n elements with k cycles, with c(0,0)=1 and c(n,k)=0 outside 0<=k<=n. For each integer k>=1 there exists an integer N_k>=k+1 such that D_k(n)=c(n,k)^2-c(n-1,k)c(n+1,k) is nonnegative for every integer 1<=n<N_k and strictly negative for every integer n>=N_k. Hence the full weak-inequality assertion frozen in source.md holds. The proof establishes the sufficient inequality q_k(n)-2q_k(n+1)+q_k(n+2)>=0 for every n>=k>=1, where q_k(n)=c(n,k-1)/c(n,k); it is strict for k>=2 and an equality for k=1. An admissible finite threshold is N_k=1+min{j>=k:q_k(j)-q_k(j+1)<1}.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
